<title>JAPAN: Advantest says sees record profits in 96/97, 97/98.</title>
<headline>Advantest says sees record profits in 96/97, 97/98.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advantest Corp said on Monday that its parent current profits would rise to a record 38.6 billion yen in the year to March 31, 1997, up 20.2 percent from the previous business year.</p>
<p>A company official also said Advantest expected its parent current profits to rise 16.6 percent in 1997/98 to a record 45 billion yen.</p>
<p>In 1996/97, sales of semiconductor testing devices and measuring instruments for mobile phones were brisk, the official said.  </p>
<p>The latest forecast for Advantest's parent earnings for 1996/97 provided by the company official was as follows:</p>
<p>(in billions of yen )</p>
<p>			   LATEST	   COMPARISON WITH</p>
<p> (Parent)	     FORECAST	  ACTUAL YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Sales		154.4		 +13.7 pct</p>
<p> Operating	   36.7		 +14.7 pct</p>
<p> Current	     38.6		 +20.2 pct</p>
<p> Net		   21.1		 +38.8 pct</p>
<p>Value of orders won in 1997/98 -- 186.4 bln yen</p>
<p>The latest forecast for group earnings for 1996/97 was as follows:</p>
<p>(in billions of yen)</p>
<p>			  LATEST	   COMPARISON WITH</p>
<p> (Group)	     FORECAST	  ACTUAL YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Sales		161.2		 +10.2 pct</p>
<p> Operating	   44.8		 +13.7 pct</p>
<p> Current	     45.1		 +14.5 pct</p>
<p> Net		   24.7		 +24.1 pct</p>
<p>The latest forecast for parent earnings for 1997/98  was as follows:</p>
<p>(in billions of yen)</p>
<p>						COMPARISON WITH</p>
<p> (Parent)	     FORECAST	  ESTIMATED YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Sales		 180.0		+16.6 pct</p>
<p> Current		45.0		+16.6 pct</p>
<p>The latest forecast for group earnings for 1997/98 was as follows:</p>
<p>(in billions of yen)</p>
<p>					     COMPARISON WITH</p>
<p> (Group)	     FORECAST	  ESTIMATED YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Sales		195.0		 +21.0 pct</p>
<p> Current	     52.5		 +16.4 pct</p>
<p> Net		   29.0		 +17.4 pct</p>
